# Bundler installs fastlane's gems here, never into the system Ruby.
# Homebrew's Ruby keeps its gem files read-only, so a plain `bundle install`
# dies on `Permission denied ... rdoc_plugin.rb`; `bundle config set --local
# path vendor/bundle` is the fix, and it writes .bundle/config. Both stay out
# of git: CI pins its own Ruby through ruby/setup-ruby and must keep resolving
# gems its own way.
.bundle/
vendor/
